{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling: the small waiting heads take one gate together. This act\nreplaces their places in the gate order of 9a1fccd7.\n\nThe fact. C1 needed 121 minutes from the R1 landing to its own\nlanding. The gate script ran 18 of them. Twelve heads wait, and each\nlanding makes the others merge main again.\n\nOne combined head, in the form of IE-1 with FG-1:\n\n| Part | Source | Files |\n|---|---|---|\n| PG-1 | 4ac92393 | 5 |\n| H1 with LV1 | 215b907d | 47 |\n| HL-1 | 6811566e | 11 |\n| CUT-A2 | 41ce712b | 3 |\n| CTL-1 | plan 1765eab8 | not built |\n\n1. The four built parts share no file outside `notes/`. Merge them on\n   the main that holds the R2 Grow head. Add CTL-1 when its source\n   compiles before the merge, otherwise CTL-1 follows alone.\n2. Each part compiles and passes its changed test files as a\n   development check under 07cd5911 before the merge.\n3. One focused interval, one gate and one review request for the\n   combined head. The request lists each part with its original\n   request and promise. One note states the evidence one time.\n4. A failure names its part. That part leaves the head, and the rest\n   goes to the gate again.\n5. Gate order from now: R2 Grow, then this combined head, then NF-5,\n   then C2, C3, RV-1, CB-1, AE-1 and P1. NF-5 moves behind the\n   combined head because it still owes five kinds of work, and C2\n   needs PG-1 on main.\n\nWhen NF-5 is ready for its gate before the combined head is, NF-5\ngoes first. Tell me in one line which head takes the slot.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}